---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Swap from "../components/Swap.astro";
import Transfer from "../components/Transfer.astro";
import Results from "../components/Results.astro";
import M from "../components/M.astro";
// Not `meta`: Vite's dev SSR transform confuses that binding with import.meta.
import paper from "../data/meta.json";
import hero from "../data/hero.json";
import transfer from "../data/transfer.json";
import { links } from "../config.mjs";
import intro from "../assets/figures/intro-psi.png";
import encodingFigure from "../assets/figures/encoding-transfer.png";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const s = hero.setup;
const model = s.model.split("/").pop();
const [mainTitle, subTitle] = paper.title.split(/:\s*/);
const sections = [
  { id: "swap", label: ["The", "Swap"] },
  { id: "method", label: ["The", "Method"] },
  { id: "transfer", label: ["Position or", "Symbol?"] },
  { id: "results", label: ["Key", "Numbers"] },
  { id: "cite", label: ["Cite"] },
];
const icons = {
  paper: "M4 1.5h5.5L13 5v9.5H4zM9.5 1.5V5H13M6 8h5M6 10.5h5",
  arxiv: "M2.5 13.5 8 2.5l5.5 11M4.5 9.5h7",
  code: "M5.5 4 1.5 8l4 4M10.5 4l4 4-4 4",
};
const buttons = [
  { key: "paper", label: "Paper" },
  { key: "arxiv", label: "arXiv" },
  { key: "code", label: "Code" },
] as const;
---
<Base title={paper.title} description="PSI localizes a causal variable in a frozen language model from the list of answers the variable can produce, with targets read from the model itself.">
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="wrap topbar-inner">
      <a class="brand" href={`${base}/`} aria-label="Back to the top"><M t={String.raw`\Psi`} /></a>
      <nav class="overview" aria-label="Sections">
        <ol>
          {sections.map((sec) => (
            <li><a href={`#${sec.id}`} data-section={sec.id}><span class="label">{sec.label.map((l) => <span>{l}</span>)}</span><span class="dot" /></a></li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <div class="theme seg" role="group" aria-label="Colour theme">
        <button type="button" data-theme-choice="light" aria-pressed="false">light</button>
        <button type="button" data-theme-choice="dark" aria-pressed="true">dark</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="title-block wrap">
      <h1>{mainTitle}</h1>
      {subTitle && <p class="subtitle">{subTitle}</p>}
      <p class="authors">{paper.authors.map((a, i) => <span>{a.name}{i < paper.authors.length - 1 ? ", " : ""}</span>)}</p>
      <p class="affiliation">{[...new Set(paper.authors.map((a) => a.affiliation))].join(", ")}</p>
      <div class="links">
        {buttons.map((b) => (
          <a class="button" href={links[b.key].href} data-placeholder={String(links[b.key].placeholder)}>
            <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d={icons[b.key]} fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /></svg>
            {b.label}
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="tagline">
        PSI (<M t={String.raw`\Psi`} />) finds the subspace of a frozen language model's activations that carries a variable you
        name, given only the list of answers that variable can produce. The training targets are the model's own
        output distributions on random pairs of prompts, so no labels are needed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block hero" id="swap">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="rule-label">one interchange, on a real pair of test prompts</div>
        <Swap />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" id="method">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="slide-title">From an Answer List to a Subspace</h2>
        <p class="slide-sub">The investigator writes the first step. The frozen model supplies everything numerical.</p>
        <ol class="method-steps">
          <li>
            <div class="step-head"><span class="step-num">1.</span><h3>Declare the answer list</h3></div>
            <p>A semantic program lists the answers the variable can produce and the rule an interchange should
            follow. For the position of the correct option, the library is the prompt's own option labels and the rule
            is the full swap: the base should read as the source does.</p>
            <M display t={String.raw`\mathcal{P} = (\mathcal{O}, \mathcal{T})`} />
            <M display t={String.raw`\mathcal{O}(\mathbf{x}) = \big(o_1(\mathbf{x}), \dots, o_k(\mathbf{x})\big)`} />
            <M display t={String.raw`\btau = \mathcal{T}\big(q(\mathbf{s}), q(\mathbf{b}), \gamma\big) = q(\mathbf{s})`} />
            <p class="note donor-ink small">no correct answer, no annotated pair, no executable model</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-head"><span class="step-num">2.</span><h3>Read the targets from the frozen model</h3></div>
            <p>Pair prompts at random. The model's log-probability on each declared answer, renormalised over the
            library, is its reading of the variable. The target for a pair is the source's reading, so nobody writes a
            counterfactual answer.</p>
            <M display t={String.raw`\rho_i(\mathbf{x}) = \log p_\phi\big(o_i(\mathbf{x}) \mid \mathbf{x}\big)`} />
            <M display t={String.raw`q_i(\mathbf{x}) = \frac{e^{\rho_i(\mathbf{x})}}{Z(\mathbf{x})}, \qquad Z(\mathbf{x}) = \sum_{i=1}^{k} e^{\rho_i(\mathbf{x})}`} />
            <p class="note recipient-ink small">the reading <M t={String.raw`q`} /> is the model's opinion about the variable</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="step-head"><span class="step-num">3.</span><h3>Train the subspace</h3></div>
            <p>Learn an orthonormal basis <M t={String.raw`A`} /> at one layer and token, with projector <M t={String.raw`\bpi`} />. The
            interchange keeps the base outside the subspace and takes the source inside it; training brings the
            edited model's reading to the target.</p>
            <M display t={String.raw`\bh_{b \leftarrow s} = \bpi\, \bh_s + (\mathrm{I} - \bpi)\, \bh_b`} />
            <M display t={String.raw`\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{donor}}(A) = \mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{b},\mathbf{s}}\; d\big(\rho(\bh_{b \leftarrow s}),\, \btau(\mathbf{b}, \mathbf{s})\big)`} />
            <p class="note psi-ink small">base <M t={String.raw`\mathbf{b}`} /> is the recipient, source <M t={String.raw`\mathbf{s}`} /> the donor</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <figure class="paper-figure method-figure">
          <img src={intro.src} width={intro.width} height={intro.height} loading="lazy"
            alt="Paper Figure 1. Left: a base and a source prompt read at layer l_k, where the abstraction selects the carrier, with bar charts of the model's probabilities on the declared answers. Right: readings as points in a simplex; the interchange moves the base's reading towards the source's, and the same target can be requested with no donor." />
          <figcaption>Figure 1 of the paper. (a) The declared answers and the frozen model's probability on each,
          read at the layer where the subspace sits. (b) A reading is a point in the simplex over the answers. The
          interchange should move the base's reading to <M t={String.raw`\btau(\mathbf{b}, \mathbf{s})`} />, and the remaining
          distance <M t={String.raw`d`} /> is the training signal. The same target can be requested directly as
          <M t={String.raw`q^\star`} />, with no donor.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" id="transfer">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="slide-title">Position or Symbol?</h2>
        <p class="slide-sub">The <M t={String.raw`\Psi`} /> subspace for the answer position was trained with capital-letter
        labels. Frozen, it now swaps answers between prompts labelled differently. If it carries the position, the
        recipient answers with <em>its own</em> label at the donor's position.</p>
        <Transfer />
        <p class="small muted transfer-setup">{model}, layer {s.layer}, last token, rank {s.rank}. Greedy decoding,
        exact case-sensitive label, {transfer.pairs.display} test pairs, unweighted mean over the three
        counterfactual families.</p>
        <details class="paper-details">
          <summary>The paper's figure, with the argmax-target and DAS subspaces beside <M t={String.raw`\Psi`} /></summary>
          <figure class="paper-figure on-white">
            <img src={encodingFigure.src} width={encodingFigure.width} height={encodingFigure.height} loading="lazy"
              alt="Paper appendix figure: three 4 by 4 heat maps of transfer rate by donor and recipient encoding, for Psi, the argmax target and DAS, each with a strip of the unedited model's accuracy per recipient encoding." />
            <figcaption>Appendix figure of the paper. Rows are donor encodings, columns recipient encodings; the strip
            above each map is the unedited model's accuracy with the recipient's labels.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block" id="results">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 class="slide-title">Key Numbers</h2>
        <p class="slide-sub">Each value is exported from the experiments reported in the paper.</p>
        <Results />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block cite" id="cite">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <h2 class="slide-title">BibTeX</h2>
        <p class="slide-sub">If this is useful in your work, please cite</p>
        <div class="bibtex">
          <button class="button copy" type="button">copy</button>
          <pre><code>{paper.bibtex}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

</Base>

<script>
  const root = document.documentElement;
  const choices = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-theme-choice]");
  const sync = () => choices.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b.dataset.themeChoice === root.dataset.theme)));
  choices.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
    root.dataset.theme = b.dataset.themeChoice!;
    try { localStorage.setItem("psi-theme", b.dataset.themeChoice!); } catch (e) {}
    sync();
  }));
  sync();

  // Overview timeline: the dot of the section in view is filled.
  const marks = new Map([...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>(".overview a")].map((a) => [a.dataset.section!, a]));
  const seen = new Map<string, number>();
  const spy = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
    for (const e of entries) seen.set(e.target.id, e.isIntersecting ? e.intersectionRatio : 0);
    let best = "", top = 0;
    for (const [id, r] of seen) if (r > top) { top = r; best = id; }
    marks.forEach((a, id) => a.classList.toggle("current", id === best));
  }, { threshold: [0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1], rootMargin: "-70px 0px -30% 0px" });
  marks.forEach((_, id) => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) spy.observe(el); });

  document.querySelector(".copy")?.addEventListener("click", async (event) => {
    const target = event.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement;
    const text = document.querySelector(".bibtex code")!.textContent ?? "";
    try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text); target.textContent = "copied"; }
    catch (e) { target.textContent = "select and copy"; }
    setTimeout(() => (target.textContent = "copy"), 1600);
  });

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a[data-placeholder="true"]').forEach((a) =>
    a.addEventListener("click", (e) => e.preventDefault()));
</script>

<style>
  .topbar { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10; background: var(--bg); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .topbar-inner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; height: 64px; }
  .brand { font-size: 1.5rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--psi-ink); width: 3.2rem; }
  .theme { flex: none; }
  .theme button { font-size: 0.85rem; padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem; }

  .overview { flex: 1; max-width: 640px; }
  .overview ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; position: relative; }
  .overview ol::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 10%; right: 10%; bottom: 5px; height: 1px; background: var(--ink-soft); }
  .overview li { flex: 1; text-align: center; position: relative; }
  .overview a { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 4px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.15; }
  .overview .label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 1.85rem; justify-content: flex-end; }
  .overview .dot { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--bg); border: 1.5px solid var(--ink-soft); position: relative; transition: background-color 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease; }
  .overview a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .overview a.current { color: var(--ink); }
  .overview a.current .dot { background: var(--psi); border-color: var(--psi); }

  .title-block { text-align: center; padding-top: 64px; padding-bottom: 12px; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5.2vw, 3.6rem); letter-spacing: 0.005em; }
  .subtitle { font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.2vw, 1.5rem); margin: 0.6rem auto 1.6rem; max-width: 900px; }
  .authors { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0; }
  .affiliation { color: var(--ink-soft); font-style: italic; margin: 0.1rem 0 1.5rem; }
  .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 2.2rem; }
  .tagline { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .hero { padding-top: 24px; }

  .method-steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 3rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 36px; }
  .step-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.55rem; margin-bottom: 0.55rem; }
  .step-num { font-size: 1.6rem; color: var(--psi-ink); }
  .method-steps h3 { font-size: 1.28rem; }
  .method-steps p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .method-steps .note { margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .method-steps :global(.katex-display) { font-size: 0.95em; margin: 0.45em 0; }
  .method-figure { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; }

  .transfer-setup { margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .paper-details { margin-top: 1.4rem; }
  .paper-details summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .paper-details figure { margin-top: 1rem; max-width: 920px; }

  .cite { padding-bottom: 96px; }
  .bibtex { position: relative; }
  .bibtex pre { border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: 2px; padding: 20px; overflow-x: auto; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }
  .bibtex .copy { position: absolute; top: 10px; right: 10px; font-size: 0.85rem; padding: 0.1rem 0.6rem; background: var(--bg); }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .method-steps { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 28px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .topbar { position: static; }
    .topbar-inner { flex-wrap: wrap; height: auto; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px; row-gap: 8px; }
    .overview { order: 3; flex-basis: 100%; }
    .overview a { font-size: 0.7rem; }
    .title-block { padding-top: 36px; }
  }
</style>
